nd (who was DFA&apos;d earlier this week) off waivers from the Nationals.</title><link href="https://bsky.app/profile/markzuckerman.bsky.social/post/3n2rnm7m6vc2g"/><link rel="related" href="https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/player-681402/"/><updated>2026-11-20T22:37:41.421Z</updated><summary>Unclassified, reported by Mark Zuckerman</summary><author><name>Mark Zuckerman</name></author></entry><entry><id>https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/team-nym/#2026-11-20T14:34:27.738Z</id><title>New York Mets offseason notes: The eight-step plan to get the Mets back in contention. Free to read:</title><link href="https://bsky.app/profile/timbritton.bsky.social/post/3n2qsm533gk2e"/><link rel="related" href="https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/team-nym/"/><updated>2026-11-20T14:34:27.738Z</updated><summary>team, reported by Tim Britton</summary><author><name>Tim Britton</name></author></entry><entry><id>https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/player-650382/#2026-11-20T02:17:04.523Z</id><title>Darwinzon Hernández: Can now confirm Mets and Darwinzon Hernandez are in agreement on a 3yr deal worth $12M, according to a person familiar with the deal. Great numbers, won title, averaged more than a K/inning while seemingly getting his walks down in NBP. Need new arms to cover a lot of innings. Should help.</title><link href="https://bsky.app/profile/chelseajanes.bsky.social/post/3n2pjflhgos2b"/><link rel="related" href="https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/player-650382/"/><updated>2026-11-20T02:17:04.523Z</updated><summary>Talks, reported by Chelsea Janes</summary><author><name>Chelsea Janes</name></author></entry><entry><id>https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/player-686551/#2026-11-19T20:53:23.443Z</id><title>Christian Cairo: The #BlueJays have claimed INF Christian Cairo off waivers from the Los Angeles Dodgers. Reliever Chase Lee DFA’d to make room on the 40-man.</title><link href="https://bsky.app/profile/keeganmatheson.bsky.social/post/3n2oxcs2xek2m"/><link rel="related" href="https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/player-686551/"/><updated>2026-11-19T20:53:23.443Z</updated><summary>Unclassified, reported by Keegan Matheson</summary><author><name>Keegan Matheson</name></author></entry><entry><id>https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/player-642528/#2026-11-12T18:00:07.222Z</id><title>Jonathan Loáisiga: Yankees, Mets and Blue Jays are among many teams in on ex-Yankee reliever Jonathan Loaisiga, who had a big year in Arizona (2.42 ERA, 1.03 WHIP)</title><link href="https://bsky.app/profile/jonheyman.bsky.social/post/3n252ejabqs2s"/><link rel="related" href="https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/player-642528/"/><updated>2026-11-12T18:00:07.222Z</updated><summary>Interest, reported by Jon Heyman</summary><author><name>Jon Heyman</name></author></entry><entry><id>https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/player-548384/#2026-11-11T17:58:18.471Z</id><title>Brooks Raley: Mets have checked in with Brooks Raley, according to a person familiar with the situation. Other teams interested, but makes sense to explore for New York given they need to rebuild and his success there.</title><link href="https://bsky.app/profile/chelseajanes.bsky.social/post/3n22jse2qlc2e"/><link rel="related" href="https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/player-548384/"/><updated>2026-11-11T17:58:18.471Z</updated><summary>Interest, reported by Chelsea Janes</summary><author><name>Chelsea Janes</name></author></entry><entry><id>https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/player-650960/#2026-11-11T01:52:35.811Z</id><title>Daniel Duarte: A minor but useful note: While some websites list Daniel Duarte as being out of minor-league options in 2027, he does have one remaining. That helps the Mets&apos; flexibility in their pen next season.</title><link href="https://bsky.app/profile/timbritton.bsky.social/post/3mzyttjmzps2y"/><link rel="related" href="https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/player-650960/"/><updated>2026-11-11T01:52:35.811Z</updated><summary>Unclassified, reported by Tim Britton</summary><author><name>Tim Britton</name></author></entry><entry><id>https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/player-677347/#2026-11-02T22:39:48.392Z</id><title>Kyren Paris: So Mets DFA Kyren Paris and Cristian Cairo, which I believe means they are back to exactly 40 on the 40-man. Will have to clear room for any additions, but they can figure that out later.</title><link href="https://bsky.app/profile/chelseajanes.bsky.social/post/3mzefdgfi2k24"/><link rel="related" href="https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/player-677347/"/><updated>2026-11-02T22:39:48.392Z</updated><summary>Unclassified, reported by Chelsea Janes</summary><author><name>Chelsea Janes</name></author></entry><entry><id>https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/player-691769/#2026-11-02T21:01:54.265Z</id><title>Philip Abner: Orioles announce they’ve claimed LHP Philip Abner off waivers from the Mets.</title><link href="https://bsky.app/profile/chelseajanes.bsky.social/post/3mze7uefcwk2f"/><link rel="related" href="https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/player-691769/"/><updated>2026-11-02T21:01:54.265Z</updated><summary>Unclassified, reported by Chelsea Janes</summary><author><name>Chelsea Janes</name></author></entry><entry><id>https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/player-701487/#2026-11-02T20:47:37.322Z</id><title>Pierson Ohl: The Mets have also claimed righty Pierson Ohl from the Rockies, according to a person familiar with the situation. Ohl was traded to the Rockies after being drafted and developed by, you guessed it, the Minnesota Twins.</title><link href="https://bsky.app/profile/chelseajanes.bsky.social/post/3mze72t5hkk2k"/><link rel="related" href="https://howlcipher.github.io/bullpenphone/t/player-701487/"/><updated>2026-11-02T20:47:37.322Z</updated><summary>Unclassified, reported by Chelsea Janes</summary><author><name>Chelsea Janes</name></author></entry><entry><id>https://howlcipher.